text:
aisha: Heads-up: we shipped the sample app that uses global fetch and some users see duplicate requests during auth refresh in edge runtimes. Repro is limited but looks like: fetch -> 401 -> refresh token -> retry triggers a second inflight original fetch. Anyone seen this pattern?

kevin: Yep. Seen that when the auth middleware isn't atomic with the fetch call. In Node undici + `fetch` it's usually fine, but edge workers sometimes retry automatically on 401 if theres upstream CDN or custom retry middleware. Could be double-retry + our SDK retry.

aisha: The SDK has built-in idempotent retry for network errors. Maybe conflict with app-level auth retry. We expected `fetch` to be a single call we can wrap. Edge runtimes may behave differently with streaming bodies which breaks our retry heuristics.

darren: Two quick fixes: 1) recommend apps pass a single `fetch` into the client so they control auth flow (`new Client({ fetch: wrappedFetch })`). 2) Provide a small helper `wrapWithAuth(fetch, refreshFn)` in SDK examples so the pattern is explicit.

aisha: I like helper approach. Can we add it to the onboarding sample app and README? Also need to document the AbortController differences (Bun vs edge vs node).

kevin: Example helper I hacked together:```js
function wrapWithAuth(origFetch, refreshToken) {
  let refreshing = null;
  return async (input, init) => {
    const res = await origFetch(input, init);
    if (res.status !== 401) return res;
    if (!refreshing) refreshing = refreshToken().finally(() => { refreshing = null; });
    await refreshing;
    // after token refreshed, retry once
    return origFetch(input, init);
  };
}
```
Note: keep retries to one, and avoid SDK-level automatic retries if app handles auth.

darren: Typing note: don't force `lib.dom` in tsconfig for consumers. Use an exported minimal FetchLike: `type FetchLike = (input: any, init?: any) => Promise<any>` and a separate `fetch-dom.d.ts` re-export for strict typing. Document both in README.

aisha: Good. Also add a short smoke test: sample app runs against Node+undici, Bun, and a tiny edge emu to catch double-request regressions. CI should fail if more than 1 retry occurs for the same original request id.

doc-bot: created issue #1245 `sdk: sample-app auth-wrap helper + fetch compat smoke` and added to the onboarding milestone.

kevin: One more gotcha: streaming request bodies can't be reused on retry. If we retry make sure we either clone buffers or only retry idempotent GET/HEAD/PUT with buffered bodies. Add note in helper.

aisha: I'll update the sample app, add the helper, and PR. Tagging @kevin @darren for review. Thanks. :raised_hands:
